WEBVTT

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>Why is the Kumamoto Daiichi 
team that passed us scattered?</i>

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.570
<i>Did something happen to the lead pack?</i>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.530
Maybe Kumamoto Daiichi got 
exhausted and fell behind.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.960
Either way, it's not a problem.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.890
As long as Hakone Academy and Kyoto Fushimi 
are up ahead, Onoda-san can still fight.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:39.470
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:03.530
<i>LINE.18  Naruko's Determination</i>

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:16.280
Team Sohoku was supposed to have 
fallen behind on the first climb.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.910
I've never seen anyone come back 
after taking a beating like that.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:21.950
And...

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.940
What are you doing back there, orange?

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.790
I've got God on my side, pig!

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.220
We caught up to Hakone Academy
 and Kyoto Fushimi!

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.950
Now we're back to square one!

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.810
Yeah!

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:40.800
<i>Square one...</i>

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.470
I caught up, Manami-kun!

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.430
Hey. You came, Sakamichi-kun.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.260
I got permission to go ahead of the group.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.150
They told me to compete 
for the mountain result.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.150
We can race.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.490
Let's go, Manami-kun,

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.610
to the very top of that mountain!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.520
<i>He climbed back up here to race?</i>

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.310
<i>And he can afford to enjoy that 
competition at the Inter-High?</i>

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.170
<i>It's too bad, though.</i>

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.500
<i>Under these circumstances...</i>

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.960
Sorry, Sakamichi-kun.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.260
Huh?

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.760
We probably can't fight.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.170
What? But it's okay.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.260
I even got permission.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.050
They let me conserve my energy for this.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.270
That first-year just said 
we're back to square one,

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.950
meaning you caught up to the lead pack

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:39.220
with all your members, and we're 
back to our starting condition.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:41.030
But right now...

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:46.530
Unfortunately, we're not back 
to square one, Sakamichi-kun.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.100
Have you noticed, Imaizumi?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:52.620
Yes, sir.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.720
Junta!

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:54.880
Yeah, I know.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:56.780
What's wrong?

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.510
We caught up to the lead pack.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:01.630
Don't we just need to let Onoda-san go now?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.590
You idiot. Look closely, Kaburagi.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.280
Count the number of guys from each team.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:07.930
Huh?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.740
There isn't enough of them.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.040
This isn't the lead pack!

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.060
What?

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.420
Which means... they're farther ahead?

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.770
There are guys even farther ahead than this?

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.790
Hakone Academy is missing two.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.690
Kyoto Fushimi is missing three.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.040
At the very least, there are 
five riders in the lead!

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.290
And among them are Shinkai, 
Ashikiba, and Midousuji.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.920
Some of their teams' strongest members.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:35.180
Both teams have already made their move.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.500
The race spans hours,

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.180
but a few minutes or even seconds 
of missed timing can prevent

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.080
things from going as planned.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.140
You don't get to do what you 
should've been able to do.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.850
That's road racing, isn't it?

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:53.230
Huh? What are you talking about, Manami...

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:53.230
It's okay.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.480
I'm sure the opposite will happen eventually.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.110
Are you ready to go now, Imaizumi?

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:00.610
Yes, sir!

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:01.780
Onoda!

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:03.570
Y-Yes?

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.340
I'm changing your orders!

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.280
Huh?

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:08.730
The situation is different 
from what we expected.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:13.290
The lead pack has already made its 
move far sooner than we anticipated.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.960
We've completely fallen behind!

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.710
<i>Imaizumi-kun's moving up?</i>

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.680
You and Imaizumi race up Mount Haruna

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.830
and do whatever it takes to
 catch up to the lead pack!

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:32.400
<i>The lead pack? With Imaizumi-kun?</i>

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:32.930
<i>Huh?</i>

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.020
<i>Manami-kun...</i>

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.830
Go, Onoda!

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.410
<i>O... noda...</i>

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.130
S-Sorry.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:53.930
No, I know. Sorry.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:54.790
I know...

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.430
That's road racing, isn't it?

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:00.920
<i>Onoda...</i>

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.230
<i>Onoda...</i>

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.420
<i>Sakamichi-kun...</i>

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.420
Can you do it, Onoda?

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.130
Yes, sir!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:12.770
Sorry, Manami-kun.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:14.890
I... I...

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:19.020
I'm going!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.890
Yeah, I know.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:31.350
<i>You'll give up everything 
you've built up for your goal.</i>

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:35.150
<i>And you have to make that 
decision in an instant.</i>

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:40.920
<i>But every difficult decision you make</i>

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.710
<i>makes a person stronger.</i>

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:48.920
Good grief. If you keep getting stronger,

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:52.680
I'll just be more excited for our next race.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.500
Get up there and pull, Manami.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.370
It's your job to take us 
to the top of the mountain.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.480
I know, Bashi-kun.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.980
Wait, Imaizumi-kun.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.820
You came, Onoda.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:08.720
I'm sure Teshima-san explained 
the situation to you.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:09.640
Yeah.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.410
Right now, the only thing we can do

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:14.340
is to keep on pedaling and 
catch up to the lead pack.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:14.990
Yeah.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.200
Onoda!

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.490
What?

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:21.250
I'm sorry you didn't get to race.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:25.710
I want to race against Manami Sangaku-kun.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:31.430
I heard you make your 
small request in person.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:39.180
You seemed so happy conserving your 
energy while we caught up to the front.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:43.850
It's fine. I always wanted 
to ride for the team.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.610
I can race next time.

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:52.390
But if I can be honest, I am disappointed.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:58.200
It's all right. There's always next time.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.500
The race isn't over yet.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.290
You've saved me countless times.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.090
What? Saved you?

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.510
But I haven't done anything.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.420
Until now and during this race, 
you've saved me countless times.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:14.930
Just now, too.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.010
Huh? Just now?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:21.220
So let me know the next time 
you want to do something.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.660
I'll do everything I can to 
create that opportunity for you.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.770
Sure, thanks.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.220
Let's focus on the present for now.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.290
We'll go as fast as we can, Onoda!

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:34.530
Got it, Imaizumi-kun!

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:35.910
Hold on!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.950
Wait a minute, Teshima-san.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.550
This doesn't seem right.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.820
Does everyone want the 
mountain result that badly?

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:46.000
Isn't sending #11 and #111 way 
too much for the mountain result?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.910
Kaburagi, you still haven't noticed?

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:54.590
The second day's course layout 
is a little bit special.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:55.660
Huh?

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.490
If you look closely at the 
course map, you can imagine it.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:03.100
I wasn't expecting them to make 
their move this soon, though.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:07.450
Kyoto Fushimi moved so early 
because they're going for it.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:11.110
And Hakone Academy sent their ace because 
they don't want it taken from them.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.950
Today, on the second day, up ahead...

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:17.160
<b>Day 2
Mountain Line</b>

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:18.140
the mountain line and
 finish line are close together.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:22.240
The guys ahead of us aren't 
going for the mountain result.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:25.750
They're going for what's 
past that: the finish line!

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:32.130
If the mountain and finish 
line are close together,

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:35.620
that means we can cheer for them at 
both if we get there early, right?

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:36.970
That's good news for us, Miki.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:43.350
Huh? Did I say something wrong?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.610
No. In road racing,

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:50.900
when the mountain and finish line are 
close together, it changes your strategy.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:53.230
<i>Miki has that serious look in her eyes again!</i>

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.220
Uh, but we're in the mountains.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.380
Can't our four-eyes work really hard

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:02.450
and beat those Kyoto whatever 
guys who went on ahead?

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.500
It's not like that.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.120
Huh?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.840
If every team near the 
front sends their climbers,

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:10.690
it'll become a race for the 
mountain line, like usual.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:15.800
But if just one team sends their ace, 
then the other teams will have to follow suit.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:20.900
Normally, they'd be too exhausted from the 
mountain race to go for the finish line.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.600
But with today's course layout,

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:25.890
they could do it.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.020
More, more!

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:31.550
Pull harder, Kiriya-kun!

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.610
Keep going until we pull 
ahead of the pests behind us!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:45.330
Kyoto Fushimi accelerated again.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:50.420
<i>They're trying to maintain the gap they 
established when they first jumped ahead.</i>

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:53.420
<i>No, they're trying to widen it.</i>

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.370
Yuto, don't let them pull ahead.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.010
I know.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:03.300
Kyoto Fushimi probably plans 
to push their climber, Kiriya,

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:07.140
who's pulling right now, to the
 limit before discarding him.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.090
<i>Their climber...</i>

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.340
They're sacrificing him?

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:12.980
That's insane.

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:18.400
Mizu... Mizuta-san,
 my legs are at their limit.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:19.540
I can't breathe, either.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.950
Please switch with me!

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.070
What?

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:26.830
We've got a plan, so you know...

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.460
Please switch with me!

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.330
At this rate, I'll have to
 drop out of the Inter-High!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.960
Just power through it.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:42.750
Kiriya-kun, you can complain all you 
want once you get off your bike.

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:45.470
You have two choices.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:49.140
Either keep pulling until 
you can't and collapse,

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:54.230
or give up, get off your bike, 
and wait for the recovery car.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:56.900
Which will it be?

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.980
<i>There's only one choice!</i>

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:00.810
<i>What? Which?</i>

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.700
<i>In any case, I want to 
stay in the Inter-High!</i>

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.350
<i>We pulled ahead.</i>

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:12.290
<i>And we jumped ahead at the ideal moment.</i>

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.930
<i>In that moment,</i>

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:21.130
<i>by letting the heedless Kumamoto Daiichi
 get between us and the pests,</i>

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.050
<i>we made them drop their guard.</i>

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:25.760
Hey, Manami!

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:30.260
Kumamoto Daiichi's just getting started.

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:33.580
Fujiwara, I'm counting on 
you to take the mountains.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:34.190
Yes, sir.

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:35.960
<i>And then...</i>

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.220
Kyoto Fushimi?

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:40.440
Yuki!

00:12:41.580 --> 00:12:42.240
What?

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.290
Ise-san, Kyoto Fushimi's getting ahead!

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.240
When did they go?

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.350
But we're still in the mountains.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.950
Why did they send their ace?

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.590
Yuto, let's go!

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:52.910
Yes, Ashikiba-san!

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.300
Ise-san, Hakone Academy's next.

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:56.080
What?

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.470
Doubashi, we're going after them!

00:12:58.470 --> 00:12:59.040
Yeah!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.540
What's going on?

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:01.560
Kyoto Fushimi is...

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:02.970
You're in the way, Kumamoto Daiichi!

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:06.230
Whoa! Why's Hakone Academy 
suddenly accelerating?

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:08.720
It's dangerous. The climbers are about to—

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.350
Look around you! Move, idiots!

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:16.500
<i>Did he deliberately let Kumamoto Daiichi 
in so he could use them as a shield?</i>

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.730
Take Manami and Touichirou with you!

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:23.790
Damn it! We won't make it in time!

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:26.240
He's too good at road racing!

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.590
What should we do, Ise-san?

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.740
We'll go after them. Accelerate!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:33.250
What? But my legs...

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:36.540
Why are they sending their aces now?

00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:40.250
Aren't we going to race 
for the mountain line?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:47.140
The only ones left are you and me, Fujiwara.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:50.500
We've fallen behind the lead pack,
 and our team is scattered.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:51.560
I'm sorry...

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:54.130
That's enough, Ise-san.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:56.480
In any case, let's go for 
the finish line together.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:58.140
Fujiwara...

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:01.440
Anyway, strength matters in those situations,

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:04.940
but I guess animal instincts 
are important, too.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:06.460
You mean him?

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:10.010
He was the only one who seemed 
to be struggling alone,

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:14.330
but he saw through Kyoto Fushimi's 
plan and stuck right behind them.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.830
I felt some kind of tenacity 
coming off of him.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.590
The man who raced for yesterday's 
finish line and placed second.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:26.590
Sohoku's red bean, Naruko Shoukichi!

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:28.930
The lead pack's here!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.300
Three from Kyoto Fushimi!

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.220
Two from Hakone Academy 
slightly behind them!

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:34.100
No, look closer!

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.250
He's so small, I didn't notice!

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.230
There's one guy following them!

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:41.630
It's Sohoku's #3, the climbing sprinter,
 Naruko the Red!

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:43.690
Hey, don't call me small!

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.650
Say you didn't notice me 
because I'm so fast instead!

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:48.980
He snapped back at me while racing...

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.540
He's amazing.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:54.910
<i>Naruko...</i>

00:14:55.410 --> 00:15:00.890
<i>He's the only one who understood 
what I was trying to do.</i>

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.450
<i>His desire for victory, his obsession,</i>

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:06.710
<i>and his wild instincts...</i>

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.410
First yesterday, and now this.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:12.890
You really aren't gross!

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:17.190
I won't let them get away, that's all.

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:19.250
Not you, not victory!

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:22.070
I-I'm at my limit.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:23.950
My vision's turning white.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:26.020
Captain, Midousuji-kun!

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:30.150
I wanted to see the third day's 
finish line with my own... eyes...

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:34.660
There's no point in just 
seeing the finish line.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.660
Come on. We're lighter now.

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:42.210
Accelerate, Mizuta-kun. Let's go even faster.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:43.380
G-Got it.

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:47.950
Climb, climb, climb, climb!

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:52.630
Keep climbing until we completely 
pull ahead of Hakone Academy!

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:54.630
O-Okay!

00:15:54.630 --> 00:15:57.350
<i>Will he discard me when 
he's done with me, too?</i>

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.630
<i>No. No, no, no.</i>

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.370
<i>There's no way.</i>

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.100
<i>I'm the captain.</i>

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.980
Hey, purple seaweed.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:08.730
Why don't you give your 
assist a little praise?

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.680
#115 worked crazy hard for you.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.860
What? Praise?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.490
What's that?

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:19.870
"Thanks. Good job. I appreciate it."

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:23.470
What meaning do those words have?

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:27.770
After being self-satisfied 
over what little work you did,

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:31.420
why would you want praise 
from others on top of that?

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:35.090
There's a side to everyone 
that's invisible to others.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:38.760
If you're not polishing what's inside,
 then what are you doing?

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:43.500
This is why he gets exhausted so quickly.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:51.360
All you need in road racing 
is your own strength!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:57.370
And, Naruko, you must be 
nearing your limit, too.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.120
You can fall back now.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:03.350
Just keeping up with us 
must put you at your limit.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:05.540
Both your legs and your mental strength.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:08.440
<i>Huh? Is that right, #3?</i>

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:09.840
<i>I see.</i>

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.420
You did well to catch up 
to the front by yourself.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:17.890
You even withstood my Zakus' 
unimpressive attack.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:23.010
But there's always a price to pay.

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:27.980
Though I'm sure you're experiencing 
that right now with your own body!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.980
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:33.900
Since I'm such a genius, I might 
just make it to the finish line.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:42.120
I'm letting you trail behind us like a
 goldfish turd because we're not enemies.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:50.140
It's because I know you'll 
fall on this climb.

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:53.460
But don't worry.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:18:01.610
I'll tell you that you did a good job 
and heap praise on you at the end!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:03.010
Phase 37!

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:05.180
Accelerate, Zaku!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:07.730
Shake off Sohoku's Naruko!

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:08.350
Yeah!

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:11.010
<i>He's right. I'm almost at my limit.</i>

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:12.730
<i>But I made it this far!</i>

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:15.150
<i>I left the hotshot and Onoda behind.</i>

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.700
<i>I abandoned my team and came alone!</i>

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:23.260
So I can't just let them leave me behind!

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:24.300
I'll show them!

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:30.290
This is the flashy man from Naniwa's 
ultimate, original sprint climb!

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.790
He still had that much strength left?

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:35.840
What?

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:37.930
Hey! You're in the way! Move!

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.220
I'm doing it on purpose!

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:44.280
This is nonsense, Naruko.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:50.160
Even if you slow us down, you're just 
making Hakone Academy happy behind us.

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:52.690
Mizuta-kun, slip past him and get ahead!

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:54.320
G-Got it!

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:57.650
I told you, I'm blocking you!

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:59.470
What do you think you're doing?

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.260
Is this some kind of friendship thing?

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:03.160
Are you trying to help them?

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:08.540
Yesterday, you lost to Hakone Academy's 
two-meter-tall man because of your reach!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.110
Absolutely not.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:15.060
But if there's anything I can do with 
what little strength I have left,

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:17.590
it's slow down the lead pack!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:22.390
But why on earth are you 
doing something so stupid?

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:27.440
Maybe it's my imagination, but I 
get the feeling someone's trying.

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:30.690
Someone wearing this jersey 
is climbing up toward us!

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.650
Climbing?

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:35.220
That yellow jersey?

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:36.820
It really is your imagination.

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:39.410
You overestimate your teammates.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:44.700
Didn't you choose to leave them behind?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.420
They're probably crying right now.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.400
They must resent you.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:51.990
They must've begged you not to go.

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:58.580
What you're doing right now is repenting, 
so you can justify your own actions!

00:19:58.580 --> 00:19:59.420
Ouch...

00:19:59.810 --> 00:20:02.110
Now pass him, Mizuta-kun.

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:07.060
He's so far past his limit, 
he's started imagining things.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:08.010
G-Got it.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:11.390
Repenting? Imagining things?

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.440
Limit?

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:17.690
I'll pour hot sauce over those
 things and eat them!

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:25.240
But he's so unsteady on his bike!

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.110
I have to slow you down.

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:28.880
Someone's coming.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:31.500
I have to slow you down until they get here.

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:34.170
Damn it! I'll pull ahead of you!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.000
Come...

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:40.000
Come on!

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:43.220
How much strength does he have left?

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:46.580
Come? Who are you talking to?

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:52.930
Who is it that you believe in so much 
that you think he's coming?

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:56.290
There must be someone 
specific you're imagining.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:59.030
That's why you're so determined.

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.690
Who is it?

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:02.110
Hot...

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:04.650
Hot?

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.030
Hey, we're asking you a question here!

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:10.630
You idiots! I believe in him?

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:14.460
I'm sure he'll come. Seriously.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:17.000
I hate people like him more than anything.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.730
People who think they're hot stuff!

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:21.340
What? He really has gone crazy 
from overexerting himself.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.590
Stop wasting your time, Naruko!

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.530
Come...

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:28.860
Come on!

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:05.270
You awake, Manami?

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:08.740
Kuroda-san, Ashikiba-san... What's going on?

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:12.020
Don't give me that, oddball.

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:13.410
Quit skipping practice to sleep.

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:15.570
Oh, heh heh...

00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:18.050
The wind does feel nice, though.

00:23:18.050 --> 00:23:19.430
Doesn't it?

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:21.580
Ashikiba-san, why don't you join me?

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:22.260
Sure.

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:22.730
Huh?

00:23:22.730 --> 00:23:26.010
Arakita-san used this spot all the time.

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.510
Kuroda-san, why don't you join us?

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:29.510
Really?

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:34.220
Good night...

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:40.060
<i>NEXT LINE  The Approaching Peak</i>

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:45.060
